OTTOM RIGHT:John Morris receives refreshment from Fred Denny, with John Keown alongside. Gerry Cameron follows by bicyle.","id":"B152-43","w":"December 1963"},{"f":"crops/B153/B153-p25-ray-hall-and-middleton.jpg","c":"Ray Hall and Middleton","id":"B153-44","w":"April 1964"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p35-ray-hall-walk.jpg","c":"CARL LAWTON (left) was a well placed 7th in the Lambeth '5', while RAY HALL (right) produced one of his \"retirement\" outings to finish 24th.","id":"B175-46","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B177/B177-p30-club-10-walkers.jpg","c":"Dave King (13), Ray Hall (34), Pat Duncan (54) & John Bromley (45) look as though they've spotted the cameraman. No. 50 looks as though he doesn't know quite what to make of it. Taken in the club 10-mile walk.","id":"B177-63","w":"June 1971"},{"f":"crops/B188/B188-p01-cover.jpg","c":"Front Cover: Ray Hall, Belgrave President for 1974-75, pictured passing the 'George' at Crawley during a London to Brighton Walking Race (see page 16). Cycling behind is Don Bartliff, Ray's attendant on this occasion.","id":"B188-01","w":"March 1975"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B144/B144-p13-walkers-club-2-miles.jpg","caption":"Four of our leading walkers, Ray Hall, Ted Smith, Bob Barnes and Ray Middleton seen here together at the start of the 1960 Club 2 mile Championship. Both trophies, the \"A.J Sawyer Memorial Cup\" and the \"Don Brown\" style award were won by Ray Middleton, who is currently showing great form.","source":"B144-22","when":"January 1961"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Ray Hall in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1956–1998: 368 mentions in 71 issues, 251 race results and 9 photographs. Wrote or reported 13 items.","img":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/home/faces/p-ray-hall.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-ray-hall.html"},"legend":false}